cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SCISSORS: Single Cell Isolated Strand Specific Observation of Replication State"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  A single-cell RNA-seq pipeline that simultaneously quantifies enterovirus
  replication and the host transcriptional response in the same cells. Reads are
  counted against a reference carrying the viral genome and reporter cassettes,
  and positive- and negative-strand UMIs are tallied per cell and per template.
  Because the negative strand is the replication intermediate of a
  positive-strand RNA virus, the (-)/(+) ratio measures replication rather than
  viral load, and per-template counting resolves co-infecting genomes within a
  single cell.
authors:
